WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.650
How far is too far?

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.189
When it comes to TV, that potentially gross
line is always changing.

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:13.240
Today, you can find just about every body
part and swear word on the small screen at

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:20.390
any given time of the day, but there was a
time when TV was a bit more conservative.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.630
Whether or not they'd be shocking today, here
are a few TV moments that took things too

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.080
far.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.420
Graphic content

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:34.020
The CBS sitcom 2 Broke Girls follows the exploits
of two New York waitresses as they attempt

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:40.270
to start their own cupcake business — but
many viewers find the pair far from sweet.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:46.590
Complaints sent to the FCC about the show's
content included one woman urging the authorities

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:52.800
to review an episode that depicts a naked
doll being manipulated into quote-unquote

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.620
graphic sexual acts.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:01.720
Of course, how graphic a Barbie can be without
actual genitals is a different question entirely.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.330
Booby trapped

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:09.530
When Married… with Children premiered in
1987, Al, Peg, and the rest of the Bundys

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.690
weren't the picture-perfect family America
was so used to seeing.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:20.290
Al constantly called Peg a horrible housewife,
mother, and cook, while Peg was there to let

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:25.660
her husband know just how inadequate he was
as the man of the house.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:30.650
But it was an episode that took place in a
bra shop that was the breaking point for one

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.180
Michigan woman, Terry Rakolta.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:39.720
The episode compelled her to start a letter-writing
campaign encouraging a boycott of the show.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.900
"I sent my children out of the room after
five minutes of this trash.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.120
But decided to watch and see what kind of
low-class advertisers would support this kind

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.120
of program."

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.610
Rakolta's campaign became legitimate news.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:58.380
A few advertisers pulled their ads, and at
least one episode wasn't aired...but ultimately,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:04.380
the publicity that Rakolta generated for the
show is credited for helping it find its audience

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.660
and stay on the air for eleven seasons.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:12.720
So, you have Terry Rakolta to thank for classy
jokes like this.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.950
"Hey Bundy!

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.410
I had steak tonight!

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.350
What are you having?"

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.640
"If I was the mailman, I'd be having your
your wife!"

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.540
Raining on your parade

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.150
Never afraid to push the boundaries of good
taste for a laugh, one episode of Seinfeld

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:34.030
"crossed the line between humor and bigotry"
according to Bronx Borough President Fernando

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.030
Ferrer.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.750
He was one of numerous viewers offended by
a plotline that saw the main characters caught

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:45.310
up in a traffic jam caused by the Puerto Rican
Day Parade and desecrating a Puerto Rican

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.300
flag, causing angry bystanders to toss their
car down a stairwell.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.400
"You know it's like this every day in Puerto
Rico."

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.430
Both the comment and the flag-burning provoked
outrage, with the National Puerto Rican Coalition

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:07.120
calling it an "unquestionable insult" to the
country and demanding an apology from NBC.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.209
The network quickly complied.

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:12.069
Family Guy's second ban

00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:17.710
Once accused of antisemitism, the Family Guy
episode "When You Wish Upon a Weinstein" was

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:24.120
temporarily banned on Fox, but eventually
aired four years after it was originally produced,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:29.349
and after the show had already gone to depths
that were arguably far worse.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:35.840
However, the network refused to relent when
it came to the season 8 finale, "Partial Terms

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:36.840
of Endearment."

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:43.390
The so-called "abortion episode" was made
but rejected, with both Fox and Adult Swim

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.910
exercising their right not to air it.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:52.270
Instead, it was released it as a standalone
DVD and on BBC 3 in the UK.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:57.700
Creator Seth MacFarlane saw it as a copout
aimed at placating conservative viewers, saying,

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.370
"Times really have changed.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.090
The network is making a decision that is,
unfortunately, probably based on people's

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.310
current ability to handle and dissect controversial
narratives."

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:14.190
It wasn't the first or last time Fox would
deal with censorship issues.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.190
Everything's relative

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:21.759
Classic sci-fi series The X-Files also had
an episode banned for inappropriate content.

00:04:21.759 --> 00:04:27.680
"Home" was the first ever X-Files episode
to begin with a viewer discretion warning

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:34.349
and remained the only one to carry a TV-MA
rating, which it probably deserved.

00:04:34.349 --> 00:04:40.270
The plot follows Mulder and Scully as they
investigate a secluded farmhouse after an

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.809
abandoned baby is found nearby.

00:04:42.809 --> 00:04:48.409
What they discover are three brothers, the
younger two fathered by the eldest, which

00:04:48.409 --> 00:04:52.970
makes for a very complicated and gross family
tree.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:58.460
"When you know your boy will do anything for his mother."

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:06.110
Fox removed the episode from syndication and
only repeated it once as part of a 1999 Halloween

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:12.029
special, advertising it as "an episode so
controversial, it's been banned from television

00:05:12.029 --> 00:05:13.800
for three years."

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:14.900
Right on...

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.289
No Homers Club

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:21.840
While The Simpsons usually takes a more subtle
approach to lampooning its targets than shows

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:28.979
like Family Guy or South Park, when Springfield's
first family poked fun at Brazil, they almost

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:32.089
wound up causing a diplomatic incident.

00:05:32.089 --> 00:05:38.539
The episode "Blame it on Lisa" saw the Simpsons
head to Brazil and face all manners of trouble

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:40.409
upon arrival.

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:46.309
Homer is kidnapped by a cabbie, he and Bart
are mugged by children, and there are rampant

00:05:46.309 --> 00:05:47.710
monkey attacks.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:55.050
"The drunkenness, the ambiguous sexuality,
I've got to get out of here!"

00:05:55.050 --> 00:06:00.249
The country's president, Fernando Henrique
Cardoso, thought it "brought a distortion

00:06:00.249 --> 00:06:02.810
of Brazilian reality" to the screen.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:08.249
The Rio tourism board agreed, claiming that
the $18 million it had recently spent on promoting

00:06:08.249 --> 00:06:11.069
the city in the States was now wasted.

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:17.460
Meanwhile, a little over a decade later, the
2016 Olympics actually verified a few of The

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.479
Simpsons claims.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:20.589
Did it for Dexter

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:26.800
When a show portrays a serial killer as a
charismatic champion of justice with a pretty

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.350
sweet Miami life, it's bound to attract a
few copycats.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:37.430
In January 2014, 21-year-old Mark Howe was
found guilty of murdering his mother after

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.729
she'd been slashed more than 50 times.

00:06:40.729 --> 00:06:47.569
Howe's search history featured gems like "Dexter's
kill knife," and "what does a sociopath need

00:06:47.569 --> 00:06:53.529
to do to blend in seamlessly with society,"
but clearly not, "how to clear your browser

00:06:53.529 --> 00:06:54.849
history, you dummy."

00:06:54.849 --> 00:07:00.449
The event reignited the debate over whether
the show should be taken off the air, since

00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:05.960
it wasn't even the first murder to be blamed
on Showtime's crime drama.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:12.129
In 2008, aspiring Canadian filmmaker Mark
Twitchell, who had been going under the name

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:18.449
Dexter Morgan on Facebook, lured two men to
his home under the pretense of making a horror

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:21.539
film about a sword-wielding mass murderer.

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:25.199
Twitchell killed one of the men; the other
managed to escape.

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:32.080
And we can't forget Jessica Lopez, who strangled
a woman and attempted to "chop her up" like

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.289
the show's protagonist.

00:07:34.289 --> 00:07:36.020
Starring...Hitler?

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:42.449
Some of Britain's greatest exports have been
created at the UK's famous Pinewood Studios,

00:07:42.449 --> 00:07:49.539
but not everything that comes out of the world-renowned
studio is guaranteed to be a success.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:57.420
(ridiculous TV show theme song playing)

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:03.020
Heil Honey I'm Home! was supposed to follow
a re-imagined version of Adolf Hitler and

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:08.800
his partner Eva Braun as they deal with living
next door to a Jewish couple.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:14.840
The show, a 1990 spoof of terrible sitcoms,
failed right out of the gate.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.779
"I'm a very, very bad Hitler."

00:08:18.779 --> 00:08:24.059
The now-defunct Galaxy channel was forced
to pull the plug after the pilot episode because

00:08:24.059 --> 00:08:27.449
of accusations of anti-Semitism.

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:33.510
Writer Greg Atkinson has always insisted his
intentions were misunderstood, saying,

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:37.000
"Sometimes you can destroy bullies by laughing
at them.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:43.120
This isn't about denying what happened, it's
about being human in the face of inhumanity."

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:49.570
About a decade later, comedy fans were finally
ready to embrace the absurdity of a comedic

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.670
Hitler.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.770
Uh...hooray?

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:52.770
Thanks for watching!

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:55.830
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

